      "domain_name": "Dealer",
      "description": "This domain manages dealer and supplier information within the ordering ecosystem. It is responsible for maintaining dealer profiles including business name, contact person, physical address, email, and phone information. The Dealer domain supports full lifecycle management of dealers: registration, retrieval, updating, and removal. Dealer records are referenced by other domains—particularly the Quote domain—to associate quotes with specific dealers. The bounded context includes the presentation layer for dealer HTTP endpoints, business logic for dealer data validation, and data access for persisting and retrieving dealer records."
    },
    {
      "domain_name": "Quote",
      "description": "This domain manages customer price quotes in the sales pipeline. It is responsible for the creation, retrieval, modification, and deletion of quotes, including quote line items that link catalog products (by SKU) to specific quantity/pricing details. A quote captures customer and dealer associations, validity period, total cost, discount, and delivery location details (city, state, postal code). The Quote domain enforces business rules around quote validity and structure. Quotes serve as the basis for creating orders once approved. The bounded context includes the presentation layer for quote HTTP endpoints, models capturing quote structure and line item details, and data access for persisting and retrieving quote records."
    },
    {
      "domain_name": "Order",
      "description": "This domain manages the order lifecycle from creation through fulfillment. Orders are created from approved quotes and track the progress of a customer's purchase through various statuses. The Order domain is responsible for order creation (referencing an existing quote), status management, event/activity logging (recording comments and dates for order events), and order retrieval by various criteria (order ID, dealer name, status). The bounded context includes the presentation layer for order HTTP endpoints, models for order data and order event information, status tracking enumerations, and data access for persisting and querying order records."
